overview":[{"en":"Chevron Corporation1, a Delaware corporation, manages its investments in subsidiaries and affiliates and provides administrative, financial, management and technology support to U.S. and international subsidiaries that engage in integrated energy and chemicals operations. Upstream operations consist primarily of exploring for, developing, producing and transporting crude oil and natural gas; processing, liquefaction, transportation and regasification associated with liquefied natural gas; transporting crude oil by major international oil export pipelines; transporting, storage and marketing of natural gas; carbon capture and storage; and a gas-to-liquids plant. Downstream operations consist primarily of refining crude oil into petroleum products; marketing of crude oil, refined products and lubricants; manufacturing and marketing of renewable fuels; transporting crude oil and refined pro","zh":"雪佛龍公司1是一家特拉華州公司，管理其在子公司和附屬公司的投資，並為從事綜合能源和化學品業務的美國和國際子公司提供行政、財務、管理和技術支援。上游業務主要包括勘探、開發、生產和運輸原油和天然氣；與液化天然氣相關的加工、液化、運輸和再氣化；透過主要國際石油出口管道運輸原油；天然氣的運輸、儲存和行銷；碳捕獲和儲存；和一個天然氣液化廠。下游業務主要包括將原油煉製成石油產品；原油、成品油和潤滑油的營銷；可再生燃料的製造和行銷；運輸原油和成品油"},{"en":"Petroleum industry operations and profitability are influenced by many factors. Prices for crude oil, natural gas, liquefied natural gas (LNG), petroleum products and petrochemicals are generally determined by supply and demand. Production levels from the members of Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC), Russia and the United States are major factors in determining worldwide supply. Demand for crude oil and its products and for natural gas is largely driven by the conditions of local, national and global economies, although weather patterns, the pace of energy transition and taxation relative to other energy sources also play a significant part. Laws and governmental policies, particularly in the areas of taxation, energy and the environment, affect where and how companies invest, conduct their operations, select feedstocks, and formulate their products and, in some cases,","zh":"石油業的營運和獲利能力受到多種因素的影響。原油、天然氣、液化天然氣（LNG）、石油產品和石化產品的價格通常由供需決定。石油輸出國組織（OPEC）成員國、俄羅斯和美國的生產水準是決定全球供應的主要因素。對原油及其產品和天然氣的需求在很大程度上是由地方、國家和全球經濟狀況所驅動的，儘管天氣模式、能源轉型的步伐以及相對於其他能源的稅收也發揮著重要作用。法律和政府政策，特別是稅收、能源和環境領域的法律和政府政策，會影響公司投資、開展業務、選擇原料和配製產品的地點和方式，並且在某些情況下，"},{"en":"Strong competition exists in all sectors of the petroleum and petrochemical industries in supplying the energy, fuel and chemical needs of industry and individual consumers. In the upstream business, Chevron competes with fully integrated, major global petroleum companies, as well as independent and national petroleum companies, for the acquisition of crude oil and natural gas leases and other properties and for the equipment and labor required to develop and operate those properties. In its downstream business, Chevron competes with fully integrated, major petroleum companies, as well as independent refining and marketing, transportation and chemicals entities and national petroleum companies in the refining, manufacturing, sale and marketing of fuels, lubricants, additives and petrochemicals.","zh":"在滿足工業和個人消費者的能源、燃料和化學品需求方面，石油和石化行業的所有部門都存在激烈的競爭。在上游業務中，雪佛龍與完全一體化的全球主要石油公司以及獨立的國家石油公司競爭，爭奪原油和天然氣租賃及其他財產的收購以及開發和運營這些財產所需的設備和勞動力。在下游業務中，雪佛龍在燃料、潤滑油、添加劑和石化產品的煉製、製造、銷售和營銷方面與完全一體化的大型石油公司以及獨立的煉油和營銷、運輸和化學品實體以及國家石油公司競爭。"}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"Chevron holds an approximately 38 percent consolidated ownership interest in Hess Midstream LP (HESM) following the acquisition of Hess. HESM provides fee-based services for Chevron and third-party customers in the Bakken. The midstream integrated infrastructure is primarily located in McKenzie, Williams, and Mountrail Counties, North Dakota, and Mentor, Minnesota. It includes a natural gas gathering and compression system, a crude oil gathering system and a produced water gathering and disposal system. Key facilities include the Tioga Gas Plant, 50 percent ownership of the Little Missouri 4 gas plant, the Mentor Propane Storage Terminal, the Ramberg Terminal crude oil facility, the Tioga Rail Terminal and a fleet of 550 crude oil rail cars. Additional infrastructure such as the Johnson's Corner Header System and various connections to the Dakota Access Pipeline provide further crude oil","zh":"收購 Hess 後，雪佛龍持有 Hess Midstream LP (HESM) 約 38% 的合併所有權權益。 HESM 為巴肯的雪佛龍和第三方客戶提供收費服務。中游綜合基礎設施主要位於北達科他州的麥肯齊縣、威廉斯縣和蒙特雷爾縣以及明尼蘇達州的門託縣。它包括天然氣收集和壓縮系統、原油收集系統和採出水收集和處理系統。主要設施包括 Tioga 天然氣廠、Little Missouri 4 天然氣廠 50% 所有權、Mentor 丙烷儲存碼頭、Ramberg 碼頭原油設施、Tioga 鐵路碼頭和一支由 550 輛原油鐵路車組成的車隊。約翰遜角集管系統等其他基礎設施以及與達科他輸油管的各種連接可進一步提供原油"}],"competition":[],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Reportable Segment Aggregation Before Other Operating","val":230789000000,"zh":"其他經營分部之前的可報告分部總結"},{"name":"All Other Segments","val":644000000,"zh":"所有其他部門"}],"total":189031000000}},"peers":["XOM","COP","JNJ","PG","OXY"]}}